; regression test: `format latex` used to be unreachable from a `.kurt` file at all, since
; `latex` is itself a reserved keyword (for the separate `latex <key> <value>` command) and
; `parse_tokenstream`'s generic `check_no_keyword` check rejected any keyword-valued token
; appearing as an argument, with no exception for `format`'s own small, fixed set of option
; names. Confirmed the break directly: `format latex` raised `SyntaxError: keywords not
; allowed inside expressions` before this fix. Fixed by skipping that check specifically for
; `format`'s arguments, which are always validated against the fixed `format_options` list
; right afterwards anyway (`eval_global_format`), so there's no way to smuggle a real keyword
; through as a side effect.
format latex
format normal
true
